{
    "name": "LDO Linear Regulator (3.3V)",
    "description": "A closed-loop low-dropout linear regulator: an op-amp error amplifier compares a zener reference against a feedback divider and drives a PNP series-pass transistor to hold Vout at 3.3V. Run a DC sweep of VIN (2→7V) to see the regulation knee (~0.23V dropout, then flat at 3.30V), or a transient with input ripple to see ~31dB rejection. ~66mA load, 0.45%/V line regulation. (Validated on ngspice.)",
    "tags": ["power", "regulator", "ldo", "analog", "opamp", "feedback", "advanced"],
